Filetype: Flipper NFC device
Version: 4
Device Type: Mifare Classic
REM UID is exactly 4 bytes (Mifare Classic single-size). The chosen value
REM 04 DE AD BE is arbitrary + safe -- no real card matches this.
REM BCC (Block Check Character) is XOR(0x04, 0xDE, 0xAD, 0xBE) = 0xEE.
UID: 04 DE AD BE
ATQA: 04 44
SAK: 08

REM ==============================================================
REM  Mifare_Classic_1k_Template.nfc
REM
REM  Purpose: structural Mifare Classic 1K tag for emulation testing.
REM  The UID here is *deliberately* 04:DE:AD:BE:EF so it cannot
REM  impersonate any real contactless card. Do NOT replace the UID
REM  with a card you do not own -- you can lock yourself out of
REM  door readers that perform whitelist matching.
REM
REM  ATQA + SAK match the real Mifare Classic 1K family
REM  signatures, so the Flipper can enumerate this file as a
REM  Mifare Classic card without complaint.
REM
REM  Block 0 is the manufacturer block (UID + BCC); we keep the
REM  bytes straight (no BCC inconsistency) so the file parses
REM  cleanly through the Flipper's NFC emulator.
REM
REM  Blocks 1-15 are sector 0 trailer + data, all zeroes -- the
REM  factory default for an erased card. If you ever fill these
REM  with real keys, treat them like credentials.
REM ==============================================================

Block 0: 04 DE AD BE C9 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 1: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 2: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 3: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 4: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 5: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 6: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 7: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 8: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 9: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 10: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 11: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 12: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 13: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 14: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 15: FF FF FF FF FF FF FF 07 80 69 FF FF FF FF FF FF

REM Sector 1-15 trailers: standard Mifare 1K access bits (FF FF FF FF FF FF = default key A & key B)
REM Sector 1 trailer (Block 19) example -- the Flipper will accept zeros here.
Block 16: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 17: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 18: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 19: FF FF FF FF FF FF FF 07 80 69 FF FF FF FF FF FF
Block 20: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 21: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 22: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 23: FF FF FF FF FF FF FF 07 80 69 FF FF FF FF FF FF
Block 24: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 25: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 26: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 27: FF FF FF FF FF FF FF 07 80 69 FF FF FF FF FF FF
Block 28: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 29: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 30: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
Block 31: FF FF FF FF FF FF FF 07 80 69 FF FF FF FF FF FF

REM Notes for the operator:
REM   - Real Mifare 1K cards have a unique UID; this template uses
REM     a fake 04:DE:AD:BE:EF. Use it to test that the Flipper
REM     emulator + an NFC reader handshake works, NOT to bypass
REM     access control on third-party systems.
REM   - Validation: python ..\scripts\verify_flipper_files.py
REM
REM   Verify with:  python ..\scripts\verify_flipper_files.py
